# ForumCore Project Rules

## Stack
- Next.js 16 App Router (`src/` directory, `@/*` alias)
- TypeScript strict mode
- Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui
- PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM
- Better Auth
- MinIO (storage), Redis (cache) — both on Coolify
- Deploy: Coolify (self-hosted), `output: "standalone"` required

## Architecture Rules
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only when necessary
- Data fetching via Server Components or Server Actions (`"use server"`)
- API routes (`/api/`) only for SSE, webhooks, and external service integrations
- Business logic lives under `src/server/`, not directly inside components

## Folder Structure
```
src/
├── app/          # Pages and API routes
├── components/   # Shared UI components
│   └── ui/       # shadcn/ui (do not edit manually, use `npx shadcn add`)
├── lib/          # Singletons: db.ts, auth.ts, utils.ts
├── server/       # Server-only: queries, actions, validations
└── types/        # Shared TypeScript types
```

## Strictly Forbidden
- Do not use Vercel-specific features (Edge Runtime, ISR, `vercel.json`, etc.)
- Do not use `new PrismaClient()` — use only the `src/lib/db.ts` singleton
- Do not commit `.env` files to the repository
- Do not manually edit shadcn files under `src/components/ui/`
